course: dictionary
lesson: 3372
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. Execution is one of them. «Under sentence of execution» is about a court or ruler deciding on a punishment, but «the execution of a plan» is about carrying that plan out.
explain: Look for clues. «The Queen goes off to see about some executions» is a serious, official matter in a story about a queen who gives orders. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Execution can also be about skill. «Great idea, poor execution» means the idea was good, but it was carried out badly. In computing, execution means the computer runs your program.
fact: Execution is a noun: an execution, executions.
fact: An execution is the killing of a person as an official punishment for a crime, decided by a court or ruler.
fact: The execution of a plan, task or skill is the doing or carrying out of it, and how well it is done.
fact: In coding, «execution» is when the computer runs your program.
fact: Many countries, including the UK, Canada, Australia and New Zealand, no longer use the death penalty.
exercise: In the story, the Queen goes off to see about «some executions». What does execution mean here? | A kind of game | A dance at the palace | A very quick swim in the sea | *An official punishment ordered by a ruler
exercise: «Great idea, poor execution.» What was poor about it? | *The way the idea was carried out | The name of the person | The idea itself | The colour of the plan
exercise: Maya says, «My program's execution took two seconds.» In coding, what does execution mean? | The program being written on paper | *The computer running the program | Switching the computer off | A list of words
test: «The Duchess is under sentence of execution.» Which word tells you that a court or ruler has decided on a punishment? | Alice | Duchess | *sentence | under
test: «The execution of the new dance was perfect.» What does execution mean in this sentence? | A tidy room | A ruler's law | A computer game | *The way the dance was carried out
exam: «The King says, "You are all pardoned," and Alice is glad, because she had felt quite unhappy at the number of executions the Queen had ordered.» What do executions mean here? | Games played with cards | *Official punishments ordered by the Queen | Sweets for the children | Happy parties in the garden
